:: Widgets DoLX Changelog [widget]
<<widget "DoLXChangelog">>
	<div class="dolx-changelog">
		<div class="dolx-changelog-hero">
			<span class="dolx-changelog-hero-icon" aria-hidden="true">&#128220;</span>
			<div>
				<div class="dolx-changelog-label">PATCH NOTES</div>
				<h1>DoL X-Change <span>v0.20.17</span></h1>
				<div class="dolx-changelog-apk-note"><strong>Official X-Change APK:</strong> Join the DoL Modding server and check the dedicated <a href="https://discord.com/channels/675158131688603721/1512272787572785162" target="_blank">X-Change Channel</a>.</div>
			</div>
		</div>
		<a class="dolx-changelog-release-link" href="https://gitgud.io/Akoz/dol-xchange/-/releases" target="_blank"><span aria-hidden="true">&#128279;</span> View the full changelog and all releases <span aria-hidden="true">&#8599;</span></a>
		<h2><span class="dolx-changelog-section-icon new" aria-hidden="true">&#10022;</span> Changes and Additions</h2>
		<ul>
		<li><strong>Added a new Whitney park event</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>While running in the park when Whitney is available, you may find other people flirting with them.</li>
		<li>This can lead into a short event sequence where you can buy Whitney a ring.</li>
		<li>While the ring is worn, it slightly reduces Trauma as days pass.</li>
		<li>The event unlocks after either completing the loft event or seeing the special orphanage visit where Whitney is pent up.</li>
		<li>Giving the ring also grants its associated trait.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added Calmoryl medication</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Calmoryl is a new Trauma-relief medicine.</li>
		<li>Taking too much causes increasingly severe overdose effects.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added instant wardrobe moving</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Players using separate wardrobes can now pay the tailor to immediately move all stored clothes to an unlocked home wardrobe.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Improved wardrobe browsing</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Added icon tabs.</li>
		<li>Added a combined over-clothes view.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added optional full Insanity effects</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>A new setting under <strong>X-Change Settings &gt; Trait</strong> can enable the full <strong>Dissociation</strong> and <strong>Visibly Disturbed</strong> effects for Insanity.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added optional permanent naturally-gained Insanity</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Added <strong>&quot;Naturally-gained Insanity is permanent&quot;</strong>, disabled by default.</li>
		<li>Normally, Insanity gained from remaining severely traumatised for over a week disappears after Trauma recovers.</li>
		<li>With this setting enabled, naturally-gained Insanity becomes permanent once triggered, and its severe effects no longer disappear through normal recovery.</li>
		<li>Unlike choosing Insanity during character creation, naturally-gained permanent Insanity does <strong>not</strong> grant doubled skill caps or permanently active talents.</li>
		<li>Gwylan's Clarity remains compatible with the new behaviour.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added more Masochism gain to Remy's whipping content</strong></li>
		<li><strong>Expanded the Water Dragon route</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Added staged Harper negotiations.</li>
		<li>Added Water Dragon sale bonuses and familiar-collar protection.</li>
		<li>Trust now develops faster during the soft bad end.</li>
		<li>Water Dragon points can grow during confinement.</li>
		<li>Added egg-specific dragon ultrasound content.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Updated the Water Dragon nest area</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>The route is now <strong>Coastal Path → Hidden Cave → Lush Cave → Hidden Beach → Stone House</strong>.</li>
		<li>After discovering the nest, its entrance can be accessed from the Coastal Path.</li>
		<li>The nest is now an Ivatan-style stone-and-thatch house.</li>
		<li>Leaving the nest now returns you to the Hidden Beach.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Water Dragon lore is no longer missable</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>The hermit beneath the castle now recognises Water Dragon scales and can tell the old Water Dragon story from their scrolls.</li>
		<li>Reaching the hermit through the castle no longer causes you to miss lore normally told by the island Elder after the ritual.</li>
		<li>If you later meet the Elder, they recognise that you already know the story and only give their apology instead of repeating it.</li>
		<li>Hearing the lore from the hermit does not unlock the Elder's recurring visits.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added Farm Racecourse race rigging</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Before placing a bet, you can visit the stable yard to interfere with the race in your favour.</li>
		<li>There are eight jobs, ranging from bribing riders to sabotaging rival horses.</li>
		<li>Each job has low-, medium-, and high-risk options.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added a Harpy travel call</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Full Harpy transformations can call for travel from the Moors to the Great Hawk's tower.</li>
		<li>Requires the Great Hawk relationship to be at Love Interest status.</li>
		<li>Also requires Legendary Hunting trophies / completion of the Great Hunting event.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Updated Melusine</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Melusine can now perform a <strong>rain dance</strong> from the plot-tending menu.</li>
		<li>Science contributes up to <strong>45%</strong> at SSS rank.</li>
		<li>Dancing contributes up to <strong>45%</strong> at SSS rank.</li>
		<li>With both at SSS, the total chance is <strong>90%</strong>.</li>
		<li>The option appears when either Science or Dancing is at grade S or higher.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added customisable lens colours to round shades</strong></li>
		<li><strong>Added customisable seed filters</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Planting menus can hide out-of-season, incompatible, or unwanted seeds.</li>
		<li>This keeps fields and gardens shorter and easier to navigate.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Expanded transformation customisation</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Animal ears, tails, horns, wings, fur, and feathers can now be recoloured individually in the mirror.</li>
		<li>Selected transformation parts can be restored to their natural colours.</li>
		<li>Existing saves preserve their natural colours and compatibility.</li>
		<li>Added more transformation-specific pet names for Avery and Gwylan.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added Gwylan's Strong Wings quest</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Gwylan can temporarily strengthen Angel, Fallen Angel, Demon, and Okami wings so they can fly instead of only glide.</li>
		<li>After doing a favour for Gwylan, ask about your wings at the forest shop.</li>
		<li>Gwylan explains that your wings have the right shape for flight but need more muscle.</li>
		<li>If you have never flown before, Gwylan points you toward the moor so the Great Hawk can teach you.</li>
		<li>Once you have learned to fly, Gwylan can begin the treatment.</li>
		<li>The ingredient list changes depending on what Gwylan can obtain that week.</li>
		<li>After you return the ingredients, Gwylan takes three days to prepare the potion.</li>
		<li>The final treatment uses Gwylan's hypnosis for the day and cannot be performed while your feathers are still regrowing.</li>
		<li>Strengthened wings last for one week, after which they return to normal and can only glide again.</li>
		<li>The quest can be repeated.</li>
		<li>Remaining flight time is shown on the Traits screen and in the Journal.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		</ul>
		<h2><span class="dolx-changelog-section-icon fixes" aria-hidden="true">&#9874;</span> Tweaks and Rebalancing</h2>
		<ul>
		<li><strong>Trait requirement fixes</strong>
		<ul>
		<li><strong>Orgasm Addict</strong> now requires <strong>1,000 orgasms</strong>, matching vanilla.</li>
		<li><strong>Cum Dump</strong> now requires <strong>1,000 ejaculations received</strong>, matching vanilla.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Tweaked Sadism</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Sadism now grants <strong>+10% damage per 100 points</strong>, up to <strong>+100%</strong>.</li>
		<li>The bonus combines additively with newer combat bonuses.</li>
		<li>Per-hit damage caps are still respected.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Combat balance: counters, hits, and body size</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Countering is now limited by available hands.</li>
		<li>Each hand used to guard can counter one attack per turn, so two free hands can counter up to two attacks.</li>
		<li>Extra incoming attacks use the normal partial-dodge handling instead.</li>
		<li>Countering becomes harder against groups, falling as low as <strong>40%</strong> of its normal chance against five or more opponents.</li>
		<li>Smaller characters are better at countering and dodging.</li>
		<li>Larger characters have a harder time countering, balancing their stronger physical attacks and other advantages.</li>
		<li>Larger characters can now properly benefit from dodge training; body-size penalties no longer completely erase Dance training bonuses.</li>
		<li>The dodge penalty for larger bodies has been reduced so training can make a meaningful difference.</li>
		<li>Smaller characters remain naturally better at avoiding attacks.</li>
		<li>Fixed intermediate body sizes incorrectly receiving the dodge bonus intended for the smallest size.</li>
		</ul>
		<p>Attack maximums have also been increased:</p>
		<ul>
		<li><strong>Weak attack:</strong> up to 15% health.</li>
		<li><strong>Light attack:</strong> up to 20%.</li>
		<li><strong>Solid attack:</strong> up to 30%.</li>
		<li><strong>Heavy punch:</strong> up to 45%.</li>
		<li><strong>Two-handed attack:</strong> up to 60%.</li>
		<li>Kicks still deal less damage than punches, but their maximum damage is less heavily reduced and should be more useful while the hands are occupied.</li>
		<li>These are caps, not guaranteed damage. Actual damage still depends on combat ability, and reaching the higher limits requires good combat skill rather than physical strength alone.</li>
		</ul>
		<p>Fighting without Extended Combat is also no longer a major disadvantage:</p>
		<ul>
		<li>All characters now begin with average fighting technique as a baseline.</li>
		<li>Extended Combat skills improve that baseline further rather than replacing it.</li>
		<li>Disabling Extended Combat no longer causes unusually low normal damage.</li>
		<li>Enabling Extended Combat no longer reduces ordinary damage.</li>
		<li>Players who prefer the simpler combat system can still fight effectively, while Extended Combat players retain additional progression and bonuses.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Updated alcohol addiction and tolerance</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Full alcohol tolerance now prevents drunkenness from weakening Willpower, blocking sober activities, or causing related skill and mishap penalties.</li>
		<li>Partial tolerance reduces those effects proportionally.</li>
		<li>Pregnancy drinking restrictions are unchanged.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Made alcohol withdrawal notices clearer</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Withdrawal messaging now makes it clearer that Stress can increase while sober.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Updated the bike</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Bike repairs can now become available earlier.</li>
		<li>Lake rides now route through the bus stop.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Updated the Updated UI</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Updated all side tabs to support the Updated UI.</li>
		<li>Fixed mobile Feat Boost spacing.</li>
		<li>Added lightweight DECOMOD previews with clearer missing-image feedback.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Improved Identity and Clothing Dysphoria</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Appearance is now treated as one clear style: <strong>Masculine</strong>, <strong>Androgynous</strong>, or <strong>Feminine</strong>.</li>
		<li>Only the style you actually match can affect dysphoria.</li>
		<li>This prevents characters from gaining androgynous dysphoria when they never wanted an androgynous appearance.</li>
		<li>Clothing dysphoria no longer builds every hour.</li>
		<li>Dysphoria is now gained once when changing into clothes that conflict with your Identity preferences, with a stronger immediate effect to compensate.</li>
		<li>Remaining in the same outfit does not repeatedly add dysphoria.</li>
		<li>Being stripped and then redressed in the same outfit does not count as changing clothes.</li>
		<li>Rejecting the currently worn style through the Identity menu applies the effect immediately.</li>
		<li>Preferred clothing now provides much stronger continuous comfort, reducing Stress and Trauma while it remains worn.</li>
		</ul>
		<p>Additional fixes:</p>
		<ul>
		<li>Clothing discomfort messages no longer claim Stress increased without actually applying it.</li>
		<li>Being naked no longer counts as wearing an androgynous outfit.</li>
		<li>Wearing only makeup no longer counts as being dressed.</li>
		<li>Existing saves correctly carry over the new Androgynous Appearance and Androgynous Clothing Identity options.</li>
		<li>Existing accepted Identity traits keep the correct comfort level instead of becoming rejected after the first day.</li>
		<li>Transgender characters keep Identity settings unlocked when updating an existing save.</li>
		<li>Hypnotic crossdressing and genderification pills still override normal clothing dysphoria while active.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Improved pronouns and non-binary wording</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Expanded natural neutral terms in dialogue, praise, nicknames, and transformations.</li>
		<li>Trusted NPC forms of address are now more consistent.</li>
		<li>Neither-gender saves are no longer reset or incorrectly treated as binary.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Updated Kylar</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Kylar now has a chance to take the player to the manor while hysterical.</li>
		<li>The dismissal event still takes priority when its requirements are met.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Rearranged Traits</strong>
		<ul>
		<li><strong>Promised Sydney</strong> now appears under NPC Traits.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><p><strong>Expanded DoLP attitude speech</strong> to 23 files.</p>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Updated blackmail tasks at the Gentleman's Club</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>The current task now appears in the sidebar beside school tasks and Avery's dates, disappearing once completed or otherwise resolved.</li>
		<li>Opening a blackmail letter now offers an option to export a save.</li>
		<li>Flower-selling tasks automatically include stall rent, so leaving Connudatus Street at dawn no longer locks them out.</li>
		<li>Landry can cancel an impossible task for a fee, but the Gentleman's Club retains leverage for future tasks.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		</ul>
		<h2><span class="dolx-changelog-section-icon fixes" aria-hidden="true">&#9874;</span> Fixes and Improvements</h2>
		<ul>
		<li><strong>Fixed Journal quest visibility</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Stone quest entries no longer appear before the quest has been unlocked.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><p>Fixed the Poppy lake typo in the code.</p>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed X-Change dealer visibility</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Residential, park, and industrial dealers are hidden while Harper therapy or <strong>X-Change Purity</strong> is active.</li>
		<li>Weekly availability is preserved, allowing a dealer to reappear after temporary therapy expires.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed divine forgiveness with temporary X-Changes</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Ivory Wraith slime penetration no longer causes divine-grace loss while the player's X-Change is temporary, including when its timer is paused.</li>
		<li>Permanent X-Changes and the player's original body continue to follow the normal Fallen Angel rules.</li>
		<li>Temporary-form virginity loss no longer applies the related purity penalty.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed consensual combat flavour text</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Consensual oral, vaginal, penile, anal, fingering, toy, edging, and double-penetration actions no longer use assault or discomfort text after orgasm or while Pleasure is low.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed NPCs repeatedly pulling modded clothes</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>NPCs no longer repeatedly pull at ModLoader skirts without making progress.</li>
		<li>Stored and re-equipped clothing correctly resets pulled-up and pulled-down state.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed autosaves and legacy save slots failing in some browsers</strong></li>
		<li><strong>Removed unused jewellery and barber-chair graphics</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Rings remain fully functional in shops and wardrobes.</li>
		<li>Existing saves safely clean up obsolete jewellery data.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Gentleman's Club rewards</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Relentless Bailey can still increase rent without limit, but this no longer turns Club quests into an escalating source of money.</li>
		<li>Normal reward tiers, rent settings, Robin's rent modifier, displayed payments, and save-loaded quests remain supported.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Gentleman's Club letter handling</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Unread blackmail letters can be recovered from the player's bedroom at the orphanage or Avery's mansion, regardless of the originally selected courier.</li>
		<li>Special deliveries from Jordan, Eden, Poppy, Avery, the Great Hawk, and the wolf pack still work when encountered first.</li>
		<li>Courier forwarding, old-save handling, quest cleanup, and rewards remain consistent.</li>
		<li>Fixed conclusion-letter errors.</li>
		<li>Expired task protection is now cleared correctly.</li>
		<li>Park-running tasks now require the correct outfit.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed virtual pet battles</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Defeated enemies no longer return after a teammate wins.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed masturbation</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Fixed an error that could occur when masturbating after using the bathroom scoop-out option.</li>
		<li>Mobile masturbation controls now keep <strong>Continue</strong>, <strong>To orgasm</strong>, and <strong>Stop</strong> together in one compact row.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Water Dragon egg laying and nest logic</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Players without a vagina or an active Omega effect can no longer produce or lay Water Dragon eggs.</li>
		<li>Extra sleep, dream, and outfit content no longer appears below <strong>&quot;Follow the pull.&quot;</strong></li>
		<li>Nest discovery and realistic childbirth routes remain consistent.</li>
		<li>Water Dragon cosmetics such as horns, ears, or a tail no longer make the game treat the player as fully transformed.</li>
		<li>Random egg laying and Water Dragon nest labour scenes now require the actual Water Dragon transformation.</li>
		<li>Invalid Water Dragon eggs are removed when loading a save.</li>
		<li>Once discovered, the hidden nest remains accessible even after losing the transformation so hatchlings remain reachable.</li>
		<li>Laying fertilised eggs correctly restarts the egg cycle instead of causing another laying event the next time the player sleeps.</li>
		<li><strong>Accelerated Brood Cycle</strong> is hidden when no egg cycle is active.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed slow body-change progress</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Progress is now consumed only when the body actually changes.</li>
		<li>If no enabled preference can currently change the body, the meter remains ready instead of resetting to 0%.</li>
		<li>The Statistics screen now shows when body changes are paused by pregnancy, ear slime, an active X-Change pill, or a neutral identity target.</li>
		<li>Genitals present during an incomplete transition work with normal pregnancy and impregnation mechanics.</li>
		<li>Body changes can reverse when Identity moves back toward non-binary.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed NPC X-Change pill scenes</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Avery reacts only after actually giving the player a pill.</li>
		<li>Pregnancy and pill protection are respected across NPC pill scenes.</li>
		<li>NPCs give the correct Continue and Choice Reversal pills.</li>
		<li>Fixed mismatched transformation narration and pill tracking.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed modded clothing storage and restoration</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Modded clothing no longer returns from the wardrobe with part of an outfit missing, such as two-piece dresses losing their skirt.</li>
		<li>Mod clothes receive missing clothing data when the game starts so they remain properly worn and positioned after storage.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed X-Change appearance restoration</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>X-Change pills no longer reroll hair and face every time the player transforms or changes back.</li>
		<li>Each body's appearance is generated once and remembered.</li>
		<li>Switching bodies restores the correct saved appearance.</li>
		<li><strong>&quot;Enable face changes for pills&quot;</strong> now works correctly; disabling it prevents pills from changing the face.</li>
		<li>Masturbation scenes no longer keep treating the player as holding a penis or vagina after a transformation removes it; the scene releases it automatically.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed meds UI</strong></li>
		<li><strong>Fixed lake-student departure timing</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Lake students no longer disappear at 19:45 before their 20:00 group departure event.</li>
		<li>They remain at the Lake Shore through 20:00.</li>
		<li>At 20:00, <strong>Hang out</strong> is replaced by <strong>Go with them</strong>.</li>
		<li>They disappear normally after 21:00.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Avery's evening schedule and dialogue</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Avery no longer skips evening returns, greetings, demands, or bedtime attention after time jumps past midday.</li>
		<li>Time passing now processes each hour correctly, preventing missed Avery events and accidental double progression of cycles or pregnancy.</li>
		<li>Avery's evening schedule is set at the beginning of each day so it cannot be skipped.</li>
		<li>Existing saves repair themselves from the next day onward.</li>
		<li>Avery stops calling the player <strong>&quot;girl&quot;</strong> or <strong>&quot;doll&quot;</strong> after becoming affectionate enough and uses fonder pet names, including several new ones.</li>
		<li>Consensual sleep-sex endings no longer incorrectly show distress text such as trembling with anger and arousal.</li>
		<li>Willing scenes show distress only when Stress or Trauma is high; otherwise, the player simply tries to return to sleep.</li>
		<li>Fighting Avery off continues to use the distress text normally.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Whitney's orphanage special scenes</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Prevented a crash during the alleyway oral scene.</li>
		<li>Encounters and endings now match Whitney's current anatomy.</li>
		<li>Interrupted encounters no longer play completed endings.</li>
		<li>The one-time cuddle scene no longer repeats forever.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed hermaphrodite body recognition</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Characters with both sets of genitals are correctly recognised throughout the game instead of being treated only according to original sex.</li>
		<li>Naked descriptions account for both chest and genitals.</li>
		<li>NPCs who see the player's body can correctly identify a hermaphrodite body.</li>
		<li>Gwylan, Kylar, Whitney, Robin, the swimming teacher, the farm hitchhiker, and the water-balloon drive-by react correctly.</li>
		<li>Hermaphrodite characters are no longer treated as crossdressing, preventing incorrect Stress from Crossdresser and gender-anxious traits.</li>
		<li>Hermaphrodite and androgynous bodies are handled separately, preventing outfits from accidentally overwriting recorded body type.</li>
		<li>The game correctly remembers the previous body when using hermaphrodite X-Change pills.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed the poster in Alex's cottage</strong></li>
		<li><strong>Fixed dance jobs getting stuck</strong></li>
		<li><strong>Fixed character descriptions</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>The <strong>&quot;You are...&quot;</strong> description now uses gender identity instead of guessing gender from the body.</li>
		<li>Pills correctly say whether a body change moves the player closer to or further from their gender.</li>
		<li>Non-binary characters are described as <strong>&quot;trans enby&quot;</strong> instead of <strong>&quot;trans girl&quot;</strong> or <strong>&quot;trans boy&quot;</strong>.</li>
		<li>Body changes use straightforward <strong>feminised</strong> or <strong>masculinised</strong> wording where appropriate.</li>
		<li>Descriptions no longer become reversed after a permanent body change.</li>
		<li>Incubus/Succubus trait naming now uses the same corrected gender information.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed forced orgasms</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Scenes that previously checked the old hidden Arousal stat now use the visible Pleasure bar.</li>
		<li>This prevents forced orgasms while visible Pleasure is still low or reads <strong>&quot;You feel normal,&quot;</strong> including during heat, rut, or with male bodies.</li>
		<li>Updated scenes include:<ul>
		<li>Farm barn.</li>
		<li>Photography job.</li>
		<li>Tentacle forest.</li>
		<li>Forest shop orgasm event.</li>
		<li>Passing out during street sex.</li>
		<li>Childbirth.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li>Fixed the street-sex passout check sometimes failing because it required an exact Pleasure value.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Brown Fox NNPC display</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Brown Fox scenes now use masked NNPC portraits, including multi-character events.</li>
		<li>Ordinary Gwylan scenes retain their normal appearance.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Alex's hungover morning event</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Alex can sleep in after a heavy night up to once per week.</li>
		<li>At 5:00 a.m. in the cottage, the player hears Alex snoring and no breakfast or tea is prepared.</li>
		<li>Going to the farmyard between 6:00 and 6:20 can trigger the scene.</li>
		<li>The event does not occur if Alex has already been seen awake that morning or the player slept in Alex's bed.</li>
		<li>Picking the farmhouse lock correctly checks and trains Skulduggery.</li>
		<li>Fixed incorrect pronouns when helping Alex out of bed after sex.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Water Dragons drowning during underwater combat</strong></li>
		<li><strong>Fixed sleep orgasms</strong></li>
		<li><strong>Fixed the Bike Depot</strong></li>
		<li><strong>Fixed NPC undressing options</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>NPCs no longer offer to remove clothing that is already out of the way, such as lifted shirts or shorts already moved aside.</li>
		<li>Undressing options appear only when something remains to be removed.</li>
		<li>Knocked-down enemies are no longer treated as naked while still dressed and will undress properly before sex.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed the manual Journal</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Typing in Notes no longer activates game shortcuts or accidentally changes passage.</li>
		<li>Notes save to the correct page more reliably, even if the game changes passage during saving.</li>
		<li>Notes no longer disappear when going back in history or reloading.</li>
		<li>Clearing all text from a page correctly saves it as empty.</li>
		<li>Deleting a Notes page now asks for confirmation.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed orgasm Stress handling</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Combat hits now apply their intended Stress instead of only 10%.</li>
		<li>Repeated orgasms during non-consensual sex no longer cause incoming Stress to disappear entirely.</li>
		<li>Drunkenness no longer turns those situations into unintended Stress reduction.</li>
		<li>The NPC multi-orgasm setting now provides only a small reduction to non-consensual Stress instead of cutting it in half.</li>
		<li>Orgasm Stress relief now diminishes with each climax during the same encounter.</li>
		<li>The first orgasm still provides strong relief, while repeated orgasms become progressively less helpful and can eventually leave the player more stressed.</li>
		<li>Orgasm Addict still handles repeated orgasms better than other characters but can no longer ignore their effects completely.</li>
		<li>Fixed Breeder and Omega pills causing creampie orgasms to remove far too much Stress because of an incorrect <strong>x80</strong> multiplier.</li>
		<li>Their other Stress-related effects are unchanged.</li>
		<li>Updated the Orgasm Addict trait description to match the new behaviour.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed missing NPC in Bailey event</strong></li>
		</ul>
